<http://data.silknow.org/object/13825d10-b7b2-34bf-970b-fccdb548baa3/observation/1>
        a                   crmsci:S4_Observation ;
        ecrm:P2_has_type    <http://data.silknow.org/observation/general-observation> ;
        ecrm:P3_has_note    "Voided velvet panel, showing a renaissance building in a garden setting. Woven with red, green and gold-colored silks. Velvet pile is cut and uncut giving a three dimensional and modeled effect. Ground possibly may have been of silver-glit threads, fragments of which remain. Continuous border on four sides of undulating floral vine. Condition excellent. Selvedges remain on top and bottom."@en ;
        crmsci:O8_observed  <http://data.silknow.org/object/13825d10-b7b2-34bf-970b-fccdb548baa3> .

